 "preamble": "Level Definitions & Target Audience Analysis:\n   Target Level: A1-A2 (Beginner)\n   Target Audience: Elementary school students or absolute beginners.\n   Lexical Constraint: High-frequency words only.\n   Grammar Constraint: Simple Present and Simple Past tense ONLY. No passive voice.\n   Sentence Structure: Maximum 10-12 words per sentence. Subject-Verb-Object order only.\n   Topic: The construction of the Great Wall of China (stripped of abstract concepts).\n   Mandatory Keywords: China, wall, construction, defense.",
 "old_transcript": "Level Definitions & Target Audience Analysis:\n   Target Level: A1-A2 (Beginner)\n   Target Audience: Elementary school students or absolute beginners.\n   Lexical Constraint: High-frequency words only.\n   Grammar Constraint: Simple Present and Simple Past tense ONLY. No passive voice.\n   Sentence Structure: Maximum 10-12 words per sentence. Subject-Verb-Object order only.\n   Topic: The construction of the Great Wall of China (stripped of abstract concepts).\n   Mandatory Keywords: China, wall, construction, defense.\n\nLong ago, people in China made a very big wall. They needed a wall for defense. Enemies came to hurt them. The wall kept the people safe. \n\nMany men worked on the construction. They carried heavy rocks up the high hills. They put mud and stones together. The work took a very long time. It was hard work every day. \n\nThe long wall went over mountains and hills. It looked like a big sleeping dragon. Today, many people walk on the old wall. They look at the pretty views. It is a very famous place now.",
